From 4595739baeedf684cc0c81adfb15a4011af33ede Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GameBuddy <gamebuddy@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:34:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] pi-plugin: one Host-owned assembly seam for SillyTavern
 preset segments

kind: additive
added-lines: 45
modified-lines: 0
extension-point: assemblePresetSegments
extension-point: presetSegments
seam-file: packages/pi-plugin/src/context-handler.ts

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

GameBuddy imports SillyTavern presets verbatim - they are read-only Host data (prompt_order,
markers, injection_depth, macros) kept bit-for-bit, never flattened. The ONE authority for
assembling the outgoing message array is this package, so a preset cannot be honoured anywhere
else without creating a second order decision and busting the KV-cache prefix the package
maintains (design/architecture/tavern-preset-compatibility.md sections 2.3 and 3). This patch
adds the single seam the Host needs and nothing more: the vendor learns no preset semantics, the
Host renders before/after/depth and receives back the array to serve.

WHERE IT IS, AND WHY THERE

The seam is called at the last exit of the Pi context handler, beside
appendPostHistoryInstructions, which already sits in that position for exactly this class of
per-turn Host text. Same safety property, explicitly: at the last exit, so preset bytes cannot
reach m[0]/m[1], the fold, any cache key, the tail-hygiene baseline, the LKG snapshot or the
token accounting - those all measured the transcript as it stood, and a preset segment is not
transcript. It runs BEFORE the card's closing direction, which must stay the last text of the
request.

WHY TWO OPTIONAL FIELDS (the design's 30-line target is exceeded)

Design section 3.1 fixes the signature assemblePresetSegments?(input: { messages, before, after,
depth }) => { messages, prefixHash } and targets <=30 diff lines as "one call site + one optional
field + one type". This patch is 45 added lines and 0 modified lines. The published signature
promises before, after and depth, but this package assembles no such buckets - they are
Host-rendered - so the call site has nothing to pass for those three keys unless the pass also
carries them. presetSegments is that carrier, and it is the minimum: a second closure that
supplied the segments at call time is more machinery for the same one fact, and dropping the
three keys from the input would break the signature section 3.1 fixes for the Host side. Both
fields ride the options object the handler already resolves once per pass
(context-handler.ts: options = baseOptions.resolveForProject?.(projectDirectory) ?? baseOptions),
so no registry, singleton or publication step was added to this package.

ADDITIVE, MEASURABLY

Zero modified lines. Both fields are optional; the call site is guarded by both; the fallback is
the existing outputMessages. With either field absent nothing executes and Pi receives the
identical array - same reference, same bytes.

UPGRADE NOTE

If upstream ever ships an assembly seam of its own, delete this patch: the gate
(tools/check-vendor-patches-apply.mjs) asserts each declared extension point is ABSENT without
the patch, so its removal turns that assertion red and names the point.

